job-mix: one job is one of 7 kinds (16 per round, 8 rounds per task per subrun); see crates/job_mix for the mix and what it deliberately leaves out
job-mix: this measures THIS kernel under multi-tasking load; it compares nothing against an event kernel and does not decide design/decisions/0096-process-kernel-or-event-kernel.md
job-mix: each point is the median of 21 repeats, with the fastest and slowest beside it (since 2026-09-19); a transcript before that date printed the best of 3 as ticks= and jpm=, which is a different statistic from a different mix and is not comparable with jpm_median=
